IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part VIII of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Transitional matters, sections 73 to 78.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- The commencement days of the amending Acts that these sections speak of are not in the text: they are inputs.
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Division 1: Justice Legislation Amendment Act 2006 (sections 73 and 74)`

-- Where, immediately before the section commenced, a reference in an Act to regulations was construed as a reference to rules or by-laws because of the former definition in section 18,
-- the reference is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws if the context permits or requires, despite the repeal of the definition.
-- src:899 | (1) This section applies if, immediately before the commencement of this section, a reference in an Act to regulations is construed as a reference to rules or by-laws because of the definition of regulations in section 18 as in force immediately before the commencement.
-- src:900 | (2) Despite the repeal of the definition, the reference is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws if the context permits or requires.
@ref s 73 (src:899-900)
GIVEN `immediately before the commencement of section 73 the reference in the Act to regulations was construed as a reference to rules or by-laws because of the definition of regulations in section 18 as then in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context permits or requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73: the reference to regulations is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws` MEANS
    IF   `immediately before the commencement of section 73 the reference in the Act to regulations was construed as a reference to rules or by-laws because of the definition of regulations in section 18 as then in force`
    THEN JUST `the context permits or requires it`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulations, rules and by-laws numbered under section 57 before the commencement are taken to have been numbered as subordinate legislation under section 57, and may be cited accordingly.
-- Example: Regulations No. 5 of 2005 may be cited as Subordinate Legislation No. 5 of 2005.
-- src:902 | Regulations, rules and by-laws numbered under section 57 before the commencement of this section are taken to have been numbered as subordinate legislation under section 57 as in force on the commencement and may be cited accordingly.
-- src:903 | Example for section 74
-- src:904 | Regulations No. 5 of 2005 may be cited as Subordinate Legislation No. 5 of 2005.
@ref s 74 (src:902-904)
GIVEN `it is a regulation, rule or by-law numbered under section 57 before the commencement of section 74` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number given to it` IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which it was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 74: the citation of the subordinate legislation by its number and year` MEANS
    IF   `it is a regulation, rule or by-law numbered under section 57 before the commencement of section 74`
    THEN JUST ((("Subordinate Legislation No. " APPEND TOSTRING `the number given to it`) APPEND " of ") APPEND TOSTRING `the year in which it was made`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Division 2: Interpretation Legislation Amendment Act 2018 (sections 75 and 76)`

DECLARE `Short title or reference covered by section 75(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the short title of an Act that, but for section 4(1) of the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938, would have included the year of enactment`
    `the short title of subordinate legislation`
    `a reference in an Act or subordinate legislation to another Act or subordinate legislation by its short title`
    `some other short title or reference`

-- On and after the repeal of the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938, those short titles are taken to include the year of enactment or making, and a reference by short title is taken to include the year.
-- src:907 | (1) On and after the repeal of the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938:
-- src:908 | (a) the short title of an Act that, but for the operation of section 4(1) of the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938, would have included the year of enactment is taken to include the year of enactment; and
-- src:909 | (b) the short title of subordinate legislation is taken to include the year of making; and
-- src:910 | (c) a reference in an Act or subordinate legislation to another Act or subordinate legislation by its short title is taken to be a reference to that Act or subordinate legislation including its year of enactment or making; and
-- src:911 | (d) the short title of an Act or subordinate legislation including its year of enactment or making may be substituted in any Act or subordinate legislation for any other form of reference to the short title of the Act or subordinate legislation.
@ref s 75(1)(a), (b), (c) (src:907-911)
GIVEN covered IS A `Short title or reference covered by section 75(1)`
      `the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938 has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` MEANS
    CONSIDER covered
    WHEN `some other short title or reference` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST `the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938 has been repealed`

-- The short title of an Act or subordinate legislation including its year may be substituted in any Act or subordinate legislation for any other form of reference to its short title.
@ref s 75(1)(d) (src:911)
GIVEN `the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938 has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1)(d): the short title including the year may be substituted for another form of reference` MEANS
    JUST `the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938 has been repealed`

-- For the avoidance of doubt, a reference in any other document to an Act or subordinate legislation does not fail merely because it does not include the year of enactment or making.
-- src:912 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, a reference in any other document of any kind to an Act or subordinate legislation is not invalid merely because it does not include the year of enactment or making.
@ref s 75(2) (src:912)
GIVEN `the only reason offered is that the reference does not include the year of enactment or making` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2): the reference in the other document fails` MEANS
    IF `the only reason offered is that the reference does not include the year of enactment or making` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 50(1) does not apply to a reference that, under section 50(1)(a) as it stood before the commencement of section 20 of the Interpretation Legislation Amendment Act 2018, is read as a reference to the other Act as originally made.
-- src:914 | Section 50(1) does not apply to a reference in an Act to another Act or subordinate legislation that, under section 50(1)(a) of this Act as in force immediately before the commencement of section 20 of the Interpretation Legislation Amendment Act 2018, is read as a reference to the other Act as originally made.
@ref s 76 (src:914)
GIVEN `under section 50(1)(a) as formerly in force, the reference is read as a reference to the other Act or subordinate legislation as originally made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76: section 50(1) applies to the reference` MEANS
    IF `under section 50(1)(a) as formerly in force, the reference is read as a reference to the other Act or subordinate legislation as originally made` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Example: a reference to the Local Court Act 2015 is a reference to it as amended from time to time unless it had been amended before the making of the relevant Act.
-- src:915 | Example for section 76
-- src:916 | A reference in an Act (the relevant Act) to the Local Court Act 2015 is a reference to the Local Court Act 2015 as amended from time to time unless the Local Court Act 2015 had been amended before the making of the relevant Act. This is because under the former provision, the reference is read as a reference to the Local Court Act as originally made.
@ref s 76 (example) (src:915-916)
GIVEN `the Local Court Act 2015 had been amended before the making of the relevant Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76, example: the reference to the Local Court Act 2015 is a reference to it as amended from time to time` MEANS
    JUST (NOT `the Local Court Act 2015 had been amended before the making of the relevant Act`)

§ `Division 3: Interpretation Amendment Act 2021 (sections 77 and 78)`

-- An Administrative Arrangements Order in force immediately before the commencement of section 9 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021 is taken to have been made under section 35 as in force after the commencement.
-- src:919 | An Administrative Arrangements Order in force immediately before the commencement of section 9 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021 is taken to have been made under section 35 as in force after the commencement.
@ref s 77 (src:919)
GIVEN `the order was in force immediately before the commencement of section 9 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77: the order is taken to have been made under section 35 as in force after the commencement` MEANS
    IF `the order was in force immediately before the commencement of section 9 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Subordinate legislation covered by section 78` IS ONE OF
    `regulations made before the commencement`
    `rules or by-laws signed under section 63(2)(a) before the commencement`
    `other subordinate legislation`

-- Section 63 as it stood before the commencement of section 15 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021 continues to apply to those regulations, rules and by-laws
-- until the expiry of the 12 sitting days mentioned in section 63(9) as it stood before its repeal.
-- Section 63(9) as it stood is not among the sources: the day on which those 12 sitting days expire is an input.
-- src:921 | Section 63 as in force before the commencement of section 15 of the Interpretation Amendment Act 2021 continues to apply to the following until the expiry of the 12 sitting days mentioned in section 63(9) as in force immediately before its repeal:
-- src:922 | (a) regulations made before the commencement;
-- src:923 | (b) rules or by-laws signed under section 63(2)(a) before the commencement.
@ref s 78 (src:921-923)
GIVEN covered IS A `Subordinate legislation covered by section 78`
      `the day on which the 12 sitting days mentioned in section 63(9) as formerly in force expire` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER covered
    WHEN `other subordinate legislation` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (Day `the day asked about` AT MOST Day `the day on which the 12 sitting days mentioned in section 63(9) as formerly in force expire`)
